The simulator folder is the client's balance-tuning surface (Phase 6): a headless AI-vs-AI batch runner over the engine's `sim/`. sim-runner.ts configures mirrored default rosters, instantiates a Greedy/Random policy per side, and drives `matches` seeded `runMatch`es — chunking the loop (yield every 16) so a large batch never freezes the tab while surfacing progress and honoring cancellation. All win/draw/turn aggregation mirrors the engine's `runBatch`; the client computes nothing about rules itself. The hooks/ subfolder wraps the runner in React state (running/progress/result). The dashboard screen that renders these metrics lands alongside as SimulatorScreen.
